// Two rooms joined by windows both ways: the lobby, whose arch shows the garden, and the garden, whose arrival arch is
// the lobby arch's counterpart and whose return arch, ahead of a traveller who arrives, shows the lobby. Each arch is a
// rim around an open aperture whose glass shows a window session of the other room. A door turns its traveller by its
// counterpart's yaw less its own less 180 degrees. The lobby's arch and the garden's arrival arch share a yaw, so a
// traveller walking into the lobby's arch arrives at the garden's arrival arch turned about, and the seat's view turns
// with it, onto the return arch eight units on. The return arch faces the lobby's arch, so its window looks on as a
// traveller walking through it would: out of the lobby's arch toward the lobby's spawn, where the lobby stands an
// orange wall; the garden stands a blue one behind its return arch. So what each window shows names its room. Each
// room is the verdicts plot (a ground, a walking kit, a chase rig and one seat) presented offscreen at the canary's
// capture size.

schema: "puck.world.definition.v1"

import "rooms.puck"

entry world lobby = lobby(nesting: 3)
world garden = garden(nesting: 3)
